Greetings-

Thanks for this great program!  It has worked fine for me for a couple of datasets but recently I was met with this error (specifically bold text):

No exonic targets loaded from the bed file. Check chr style.
Error in .Call2("solve_user_SEW0", start, end, width, PACKAGE = "IRanges") :
  solving row 1: range cannot be determined from the supplied arguments (too many NAs)
Calls: getcoverage ... RangesList -> IRanges -> solveUserSEW0 -> .Call2 -> .Call
Execution halted

I checked the bed file to make sure that chromosome naming style agrees with the .bam files.  The .bam files are indexed and .bai files are in the same directory as the .bam files. The bed file is sorted correctly as well.  Has anyone seen this error before?  If so, any suggestions for a solution would be greatly appreciated.

Best-

labrat

